[ar:aarav_kharade1234]
[ti:What do we do now?]
[al:Bringing the world back]

[00:00.00]So...
[00:03.15]what do we do now?
[00:06.39]I don't know.
[00:10.18]Good.
[00:16.02]The room is still here,
[00:20.60]The morning hasn't come,
[00:23.86]The world is still turning
[00:28.29]Like nothing has been done.
[00:33.60]There's dust on the window,
[00:37.23]A crack beneath the door,
[00:40.32]We thought we'd have the answers,
[00:43.05]We don't have them anymore.
[00:48.60]There's a thousand things
[00:51.09]We never got to say,
[00:52.64]A thousand little moments
[00:54.03]That disappeared away.
[00:55.40]And maybe we were looking
[00:56.91]For a place we'd never find,
[00:58.43]Maybe we were so busy
[01:01.61]Trying to save the past
[01:03.89]We forgot we had tonight.
[01:07.61]We don't know the ending,
[01:09.09]We don't know the name,
[01:10.36]We don't know what tomorrow
[01:11.71]Is going to change.
[01:13.81]But nobody has written it.
[01:17.41]Not yet.
[01:19.80]Tomorrow isn't waiting for us,
[01:22.07]Tomorrow isn't written down,
[01:25.33]If nobody knows what comes next,
[01:28.31]Then nobody owns the sound.
[01:31.36]We don't need a perfect answer,
[01:34.44]We don't need to understand,
[01:37.32]If the future is still empty,
[01:40.33]We can put something there with our hands.
[01:44.30]With our hands.
[01:47.71]With our hands.
[01:56.47]A child draws a doorway
[01:57.48]On a piece of cardboard,
[01:59.11]Calls it somewhere better
[02:00.44]And doesn't ask what it's for.
[02:02.52]Someone laughs too loudly,
[02:03.84]Someone sings off-key,
[02:05.23]Someone builds a little world
[02:06.43]Out of things nobody sees.
[02:08.45]An old man watches sunlight
[02:09.84]Move slowly across the wall,
[02:11.57]And for one tiny second
[02:12.72]He remembers being small.
[02:14.49]A girl writes three words
[02:15.75]Then crosses out all three,
[02:17.44]Starts again from nothing.
[02:19.18]Like we all secretly do.
[02:21.99]Maybe that's the miracle,
[02:23.05]Maybe that's the trick:
[02:24.43]We lose what we were holding,
[02:25.95]And still create another thing.
[02:27.81]Tomorrow isn't waiting for us,
[02:30.76]Tomorrow isn't written down,
[02:33.30]If nobody knows what comes next,
[02:36.02]Then nobody owns the sound.
[02:39.25]We don't need a perfect answer,
[02:42.47]We don't need to understand,
[02:45.28]If the future is still empty,
[02:48.56]We can put something there with our hands.
[02:52.76]Make a little noise.
[02:53.72]Make a little light.
[02:55.23]Make something nobody
[02:56.69]Has ever seen tonight.
[02:58.65]Make a wrong turn.
[02:59.72]Make a mess.
[03:00.84]Make a song that doesn't know
[03:02.78]What it's supposed to be yet.
[03:12.22]I used to think
[03:15.87]Growing up meant
[03:17.65]Finding out who I was.
[03:20.53]Then I thought
[03:22.80]I had lost myself.
[03:25.05]Maybe...
[03:29.16]I was never supposed
[03:31.53]To stay the same.
[03:35.97]Can I try?
[03:37.28]Yeah.
[03:38.72]If it's good?
[03:41.07]Especially then.
[03:49.86]Tomorrow isn't waiting for us,
[03:51.38]Tomorrow isn't written down,
[03:54.77]All the things we thought were endings
[03:58.00]Were just doors without a sound.
[04:03.20]Every memory can change us,
[04:04.57]Every mistake can leave a mark,
[04:07.23]Every ordinary moment
[04:10.69]Can become a little spark.
[04:14.99]We don't know what comes after,
[04:16.93]We don't know where this will land,
[04:20.41]But the future isn't finished.
[04:23.51]So let's make it with our hands.
[04:28.70]Make something.
[04:29.60]Make anything.
[04:30.78]Make something beautiful.
[04:33.53]Make something strange.
[04:34.52]Make something nobody asked for.
[04:36.76]Make something nobody understands.
[04:39.94]Make something that outlives
[04:42.67]the version of you
[04:44.37]that made it.
[05:23.52]Tomorrow isn't here yet.
[05:26.83]Good.
